[{:adr/authoritative_for ["90-docs/aliexpress-sedori/observations-ledger.edn is an append-only EDN event log (one map per line) of AliExpress product/seller/price observations, queried via DataScript through 90-docs/aliexpress-sedori/query.cljs — never hand-edited, only appended through 90-docs/aliexpress-sedori/append.cljs"
                           "there is no unattended, high-frequency automated AliExpress scraper in this workspace, and none should be built to make this dataset \"continuous\" — a plain HTTP client (no JS execution) is redirected straight to AliExpress's CAPTCHA/JS-challenge wall, and building code to defeat that would be bot-detection evasion, which is out of bounds regardless of user convenience"
                           "AliExpress product/seller data collection for this dataset happens two ways: WebFetch (JS-rendering fetch tool) against search/category listing pages for title+price+discount+rating+sold-count, at human-comparable low frequency, not scripted into a loop; and interactive Claude-in-Chrome browsing of individual product detail pages for seller/store name, which only works in a live paired-browser session and cannot run in an unattended cloud routine"
                           "the only legitimate path to genuinely continuous/robust automated AliExpress data access is the official AliExpress Open Platform / Affiliate API, which requires the account owner to register for API credentials — this is not something an agent does unilaterally"]
  :adr/topic "aliexpress-sedori-observation-dataset-edn-datascript-bot-detection-limits"
